OSI Model - Open Systems Interconnection (7 layers)

(bottom → top): Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away

7. Application   - user apps talk to network (HTTP, DNS, FTP, SSH, SMTP)
6. Presentation  - format, encrypt, compress (TLS/SSL, JSON, JPG)
5. Session       - open / maintain / close conversation (login session)
4. Transport     - segments, ports, reliability (TCP, UDP)
3. Network       - packets, IP address, routing (IP, ICMP, router)
2. Data Link     - frames, MAC address (ARP, switch)
1. Physical      - bits, cables, Wi-Fi signals (hub, cable)

Sending   : 7 → 1 (encapsulation - wrap)
Receiving : 1 → 7 (decapsulation - unwrap)





Each layer answers one question

┌────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Layer          │ The question it answers          │ Answer for madhukarreddy.com         │
├────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 7 Application  │ What do you want?                │ "Show me the madhukarreddy homepage" │
│ 6 Presentation │ Is it safe and readable?         │ It's encrypted (HTTPS)               │
│ 5 Session      │ Is the connection still open?    │ Yes, Chrome keeps it open            │
│ 4 Transport    │ Which app or door?               │ Port 443                             │
│ 3 Network      │ Which computer on the internet?  │ madhukarreddy.com's IP address       │
│ 2 Data Link    │ Which device next on my network? │ The router's MAC address             │
│ 1 Physical     │ How does it physically travel?   │ Wi-Fi signals / cable as 0s and 1s   │
└────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘




